<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00RY">Variant <span data-tag="00RY">2.5.7.17</span>.</a> Let $S_{\bullet }$ and $T_{\bullet }$ be simplicial sets containing simplicial subsets $S'_{\bullet }$ and $T'_{\bullet }$, respectively. Applying Theorem <a data-tag="00RV" href="/tag/00RV">2.5.7.14</a> to the simplicial abelian groups $\operatorname{\mathbf{Z}}[ S_{\bullet } ] / \operatorname{\mathbf{Z}}[ S'_{\bullet } ]$ and $\operatorname{\mathbf{Z}}[ T_{\bullet } ] / \operatorname{\mathbf{Z}}[ T'_{\bullet } ]$, we obtain a quasi-isomorphism </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \mathrm{EZ}: \mathrm{N}_{\ast }(S, S'; \operatorname{\mathbf{Z}}) \boxtimes \mathrm{N}_{\ast }(T, T'; \operatorname{\mathbf{Z}}) \rightarrow \mathrm{N}_{\ast }(S \times T, (S' \times T) \cup (S \times T'); \operatorname{\mathbf{Z}}), \]
</div>
</article>
